WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.013
This model shows the right side of a child's jaws at 6 years.

00:00:04.363 --> 00:00:06.838
Baby teeth are blue and adult teeth are yellow.

00:00:07.638 --> 00:00:11.721
Each adult tooth starts as a crown deep in the jaw. As its root grows,

00:00:11.721 --> 00:00:13.121
it moves toward the gum.

00:00:13.921 --> 00:00:14.707
As it moves up,

00:00:14.707 --> 00:00:18.849
the root of the baby tooth melts away. The baby tooth gets loose and falls out.

00:00:19.649 --> 00:00:24.235
The first adult molars come at about 6, and the second molars at about 12.

00:00:25.035 --> 00:00:29.239
Every child is different. Teeth often come a year or more earlier or later,

00:00:29.239 --> 00:00:30.753
and this is usually normal.
